      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hyaluronidase into the foreskin: 1 mL (150 U) total in 1 or 2 SC injections (avoid intravascular injection: anaphylaxis); disperses the edema rapidly. Osmotic agents (sugar, salt) on the glans and foreskin draw out edema; may take hours and should not be used in acute paraphimosis. Children may need local anesthesia and sometimes sedation."
     }
